# Heraj meem project – code and instructions

Use this file for consistent code style and to apply instructions from the project owner. Keep it updated when new conventions are given.

## Domain entities and data models

- **Where to put types**
  - Put **larger, top-level models** (full API responses, screen/feature aggregates, DTOs with many fields) in **`data/models/`** (and their domain counterparts in **`domain/entities/`** when the feature uses clean architecture entities).
  - Put **smaller nested types** that belong inside a bigger model (e.g. `User`, `TaskAssignee`, `BoardColumn` inside a workspace or task-board payload) in **`domain/entities/`** as separate entity files, then reference them from the parent model/entity. Do not inline large nested object graphs in one file—split sub-objects into `entities/` and compose the parent in `models/`.

- **Include `fromJson` and `toJson`** in both **domain entities** (`domain/entities/`) and **data models** (`data/models/`). Use `factory X.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json)` and `Map<String, dynamic> toJson()` so entities and models can be serialized from the API/data layer and passed around consistently. Prefer snake_case for JSON keys (e.g. `avatar_url`) when matching backend or DTOs.

