## Feature structure (same as settings)

Every new feature MUST follow the same structure as the **settings** feature:

```
lib/features/<feature_name>/
├── data/
│   ├── data_source/     # Remote/local data sources (API, DB)
│   ├── repo/            # Repository implementations (*_repo_imp.dart)
│   └── models/          # DTOs / data models
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/        # Domain entities
│   ├── repo/            # Repository interfaces (abstract)
│   └── use_case/        # Use cases (business logic)
└── presentation/
    ├── view/            # Screens / main views (*_view.dart, *_screen.dart)
    │   └── widgets/     # Feature-specific widgets
    └── managers/        # Providers, action mixins, screen-flow state (e.g. *_provider.dart, *_actions_mixin.dart)
```

- **data**: data sources, repo implementations, models.
- **domain**: entities, repo contracts, use cases (no Flutter/UI).
- **presentation**: `view/` (screens), `view/widgets/` (UI components), `managers/` (Riverpod providers, action mixins — **not** under `view/`).

